@startuml commit_update
title Cumulative O3 retirement -> IBPU ledger -> model-private BTB updates
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 95

participant "Fetch / BAC" as Fetch
participant "Gem5BpuBridge" as Bridge
participant "IBPU implementation" as BPU
participant "PredictionLedger" as Ledger
participant "Model-private BTB(s)" as BTB
participant "Commit / ROB" as Commit
participant "timeBuffer / commitInfo" as TB

legend left
  [E] Existing gem5 method or signal
  [N] Proposed IBPU / bridge integration
  [A] Illustrative internal operation, not an existing method
endlegend

== Keep the original lookup and dynamic branch identity ==
BPU -> BTB : [N] lookup(BTBQuery{addr=original lookup base})
BTB --> BPU : [N] BTBResult{cfi_list, commitData}
BPU -> Ledger : [A] retain lookup metadata and speculative history\n\
under PredictionKey, block index and CfiId
Fetch -> Bridge : [N] bindAndPredict(inst, cursor)
Bridge -> BPU : [N] onPredecodeFeedback(key, blockIndex, instSeq,\n\
pc, staticInst, matchedCfi)
BPU -> Ledger : [N] bind(fb): InstSeqNum -> BranchRef
BPU --> Bridge : [N] PredictionBinding{branch, taken, nextPC, needsRepair}
note over BPU, BTB
  PC alone is not a dynamic identity (loops can revisit it).
  commitData belongs to this lookup, not to the most recent lookup.
  Multiple CFI bindings may share lookup metadata; retain it until
  every dependent commit/recovery use has finished.
  A miss can allocate with commitData=NULL.
end note

== Recovery corrects state before later retirement ==
opt An executed branch mispredict / earlier frontend correction arrives
    Fetch -> Bridge : [N] forwardFeedback(timeBuffer)
    Bridge -> BPU : [N] onRecovery(event)
    BPU -> Ledger : [N] recover(event)
    Ledger -> Ledger : [A] remove younger bindings; preserve surviving \
boundary\nstore actual outcome when supplied; otherwise only known correction
end
note over BPU, Ledger
  See backend_recovery.puml. Wrong-path bindings removed by recovery
  must never be trained merely because their seqNum is <= a later watermark.
  A predictor override supplies a prediction, not an actual outcome.
end note

== Existing Commit publishes one cumulative watermark per thread ==
loop Up to commitWidth successful retirements
    Commit -> Commit : [E] commitInsts(): examine ROB head
    alt head_inst is already squashed
        Commit -> Commit : [E] rob->retireHead(); ppSquash->notify(head_inst)
        note right of Commit
          No successful-commit watermark is generated for this removal.
        end note
    else Unsquashed instruction
        Commit -> Commit : [E] commitHead(head_inst, num_committed)
        opt commitHead succeeds
            Commit -> TB : [E] commitInfo[tid].doneSeqNum=head_inst->seqNum
        end
    end
end
note over Commit, TB
  Later successful retirements overwrite doneSeqNum in this cycle.
  BAC receives the youngest committed sequence number, not a per-branch
  Commit -> IBPU callback. Source: commit.cc:954-1013.
end note
... commitToFetchDelay ...
TB --> Fetch : [E] BAC::checkAndUpdateBPUSignals(tid)
alt commitInfo.squash == true
    Fetch -> Bridge : [N] forwardFeedback(timeBuffer): recovery branch
    Bridge -> BPU : [N] onRecovery(event)
    note over Fetch, BPU
      doneSeqNum is a squash cut in this branch.
      Do not call onCommitUpdate() for that same broadcast.
      BAC returns before decode/fetch signal processing.
    end note
else doneSeqNum != 0
    Fetch -> Bridge : [N] forwardFeedback(timeBuffer): retirement branch
    Bridge -> BPU : [N] onCommitUpdate(CommitUpdate{tid, \
throughSeq=doneSeqNum})
    BPU -> Ledger : [N] commitThrough(tid, throughSeq)
    loop Surviving bound branches <= throughSeq, oldest first
        Ledger --> BPU : [A] branch identity, final training outcome,\n\
original query base, history and original commitData
        BPU -> BPU : [A] update direction predictor / RAS / indirect state\n\
according to this model's commit policy
        opt This branch is eligible for BTB training
            BPU -> BTB : [N] update(BTBUpdate{addr=original query base,\n\
cfi_result=observed/training CFI, commitData=matching lookup})
        end
        BPU -> Ledger : [A] retire binding; release metadata exactly once\n\
after its final dependent user
    end
end
note over Fetch, BPU
  After a non-squash commit update, BAC still checks decode then fetch.
  Existing hook to replace: bpu->update(doneSeqNum, tid), bac.cc:331-335.
  Legacy behavior: BPredUnit::update() walks histories oldest first;
  commitBranch() updates direction, indirect/RAS and eligible BTB entries
  (src/cpu/pred/bpred_unit.cc:336-399).
end note
note over BPU, Ledger
  There is no actual-outcome payload in the normal commit watermark.
  As in the legacy predictor, a surviving prediction is validated by
  successful execution/retirement, or corrected by recovery beforehand.
  The ledger must track the same prediction used by DynInst and execution.
  Models requiring more execution data need an explicit additional hook.
  FTQ pop/onTargetConsumed never means this branch has committed.
end note
@enduml
